# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Build artefacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Scratch output. The demo and the gate write reports under /tmp; nothing there is ever tracked.
/tmp/
tmp/
*.tmp

# Real data must never enter the repository. `data-raw/` lives at ~/code/data-raw, outside this
# tree, but it is ignored here as a guard against a mistaken `cp -r` or a wrong `cd`. Downloaded
# datasets, the Freddie Mac files, the regulatory PDFs and the FinQA / TAT-QA dev sets all live
# there. See CLAUDE.md, hard constraints.
data-raw/

# NOTE: `tests/probatio/cassettes/` is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the recorded tapes,
# which CI and every provenance claim in the documentation must be able to read.

# Study results, decided before the tree grew (D-185). A chunk of `quaestor study run` writes
# about 11 MB a cell -- the artifact store and the subject's own `run/` output -- and the study is
# 62 cells, so what enters the repository is decided by rule here rather than by whoever runs the
# last chunk.
#
# Committed: `published/`, the one copy the README and `docs/STUDY.md` quote from, and
# `first-live/`, Phase 9's archived runs that the test layer reads. Not committed: every
# timestamped working directory a chunk writes, which is reproduced by re-running the chunk.
eval/results/*
!eval/results/.gitkeep
!eval/results/first-live/
!eval/results/published/

# Inside a published run, the artifact store stays out: it is regenerated exactly by replaying
# that run's committed cassettes, and the conclusions rest on `report.md`, `findings.json`,
# `claims.json`, `trace.jsonl` and `summary.json`, all of which are committed (D-185).
eval/results/published/**/artifacts/

# The subject's own `run/` output never carries rows into the repository, in any results
# directory. A `--data` run writes the real panel to `data_train.csv` and `data_test.csv` and its
# predictions beside them; `CLAUDE.md`'s "no Freddie Mac rows in the repo" is a hard constraint
# and not something to remember at commit time. The four JSON contract files are what Phase 9
# committed by hand and are what this keeps.
eval/results/**/run/*.csv

# The seeded-defect variants of Phase 10 are generated artefacts, not sources: `quaestor study
# build` writes one package per row of `eval/taxonomy.yaml`, and the taxonomy plus `eval/seed.py`
# are what is committed. A variant built from real data would also carry rows of it, which is the
# second reason this directory never enters the repository (CLAUDE.md, hard constraints).
eval/variants/
